<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The Android 12+ launch-screen icon.

     Why this exists at all: left to itself the system builds the launch icon
     from @mipmap/ic_launcher, i.e. the 432px drawable-xxxhdpi launcher layer,
     and scales it up to the 240dp splash canvas — about 960px on a 4x screen,
     a 2.2x upscale, which is what made the mark look blurred on device. This
     points at the 1024px master instead, so the same 240dp canvas is a
     DOWNSCALE and the edges stay sharp.

     Why the inset: the splash canvas is 240dp but only a 160dp circle of it is
     visible (66.7%), while the master art spans 82% of its own canvas — it was
     drawn for the launcher's larger safe area. Insetting 11% a side leaves the
     mark at 0.82 x 0.78 = 0.64 of the canvas, inside the mask with a little
     radial margin so it does not appear to graze it.

     The inset is a percentage on android:inset, the same form the generated
     mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml uses. There are no insetLeftFraction /
     insetTopFraction attributes — those do not exist and fail resource
     linking; the ordinary inset attributes are what carry a fraction.

     hg_splash_mark.png is a byte copy of assets/launcher_icon/foreground.png,
     which tool/generate_launcher_icons.dart renders from the ConceptHG path
     geometry. Regenerate that master and re-copy it if the mark ever changes;
     nothing here derives from the launcher icon at build time. -->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/hg_splash_mark"
    android:inset="11%" />
